    anticipatedMisconceptions: ['Do not present tekkes as only places of private worship or suggest that Yunus caused the political crisis.'],
    grammarFocus: 'Targets: adding (not only … also, furthermore, too, especially) · cause and result (weakened by, caused, because of + noun) · while + past continuous passive for an ongoing background (were still being felt) · past simple for the new event · cope with.\nNotice (Activity 1): learners sort six chapter sentences into “adds more information” and “shows a cause or a result”, then say which words helped.\nBuild (Activities 2–3): choose were still being felt / took place / cope with, then say the same cause in a new way (The Babai revolts weakened …, … because of the defeat).\nLikely errors: *were still feeling (active instead of passive) · *cope these situations · *because the defeat.\nUse (Activity 4): 5–6 sentences about a real community facing change, with one while-background sentence.',
    pronunciationFocus: 'Pause after the background clause: “While the NEGative effects of these reVOLTS were still being FELT | the deFEAT at Kösedağ took PLACE”.\n-ed endings: weakened /d/, helped /t/, faced /t/, improved /d/, trained /d/.\nWord focus: CIR-cum-stan-ces, FUR-ther-more, es-PE-cial-ly, or-gan-i-ZA-tions.',
